# Doris query integration example

This is a template, not an enabled connection. Provision an actual skill in the
private knowledge snapshot only after configuring the host-side gateway.

Use the deployment's authorized gateway alias and scoped sandbox credential.
Never embed the upstream database password, private IP address, schema inventory
or customer query examples in this public file. Discover tables through the
allowed connection instead of assuming a particular business schema.

For read-only analysis, select only the necessary columns, apply bounded filters,
and stream large exports to workspace files. Observe the gateway's row, byte,
concurrency and timeout limits. Do not bypass the gateway with direct upstream
connections when authorization fails.
